.TH ZERODDS-COAP-BRIDGED.YAML 5 "" "ZeroDDS" "ZeroDDS Manual"
.SH NAME
zerodds-coap-bridged.yaml \- configuration file for zerodds-coap-bridged(1)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I /etc/zerodds/coap-bridged.yaml
.SH DESCRIPTION
YAML document describing how the CoAP bridge daemon maps DDS topics onto CoAP
resources. The schema is the one of
.IR zerodds-coap-bridge-1.0 " \(sc3;"
the parser that reads it is
.IR crates/coap-bridge/src/daemon/config.rs::load_from_str .
.PP
Top-level keys:
.BR domain ", " log_level ", " coap ", " oscore ", " auth ", " acl ", " metrics ", " topics .
.PP
An unknown top-level key is
.I not
a parse error. The daemon logs a WARN line on stderr and starts with the
defaults \(em watch the WARN log.
.PP
.BI ${VAR} " and " ${VAR:-default}
are substituted from the environment before the document is parsed.
.SH KEYS
.SS Top level
.TP
.B domain
Integer DDS domain ID. Default
.IR 0 .
.TP
.B log_level
.IR trace " | " debug " | " info " | " warn " | " error .
.SS coap
.TP
.B bind
UDP listen address for
.IR coap:// ,
e.g.
.IR "0.0.0.0:5683" .
.TP
.B bind_dtls
Separate listen address for
.IR coaps:// .
Without it the daemon uses
.B bind
with the port raised by one.
.TP
.B max_message_size
DoS cap per datagram in bytes. Default
.I 1152
per RFC 7252; raise it only behind a jumbo MTU.
.TP
.B ack_timeout_ms
CON retransmission timeout in milliseconds.
.TP
.B max_retransmit
Number of CON retransmissions before the exchange is given up.
.TP
.B observe_max_age_secs
Lifetime of an
.I Observe
registration.
.TP
.B dtls
Sub-map with
.B enabled
(boolean),
.B ca_file
(trust anchor),
.BR cert_file " and " key_file
(server material),
.B cipher_suites
(list of IANA names \(em an unknown name aborts the start instead of being
dropped) and
.B psk
(list of pre-shared keys, each entry carrying
.BR identity " and " secret_hex ).
.SS oscore
Object Security for Constrained RESTful Environments, RFC 8613 \(em end-to-end
protection that survives a CoAP proxy (\(sc7.2).
.TP
.B enabled
Boolean. With
.IR true ,
.B master_secret_hex
is mandatory; the daemon refuses to start without it.
.TP
.B master_secret_hex
OSCORE master secret, hex.
.TP
.B master_salt_hex
OSCORE master salt, hex.
.TP
.B id_context_hex
OSCORE ID context, hex.
.TP
.B sender_id_hex
Sender ID of this daemon. Default
.IR 01 .
.TP
.B replay_window
Width of the anti-replay window.
.SS auth
.TP
.B mode
.IR none " | " bearer " | " jwt " | " mtls .
A ZeroDDS extension; the CoAP bridge spec secures with DTLS and OSCORE only.
.I bearer
and
.I jwt
read the token from CoAP option 65000
.RI ( "Bearer <token>" ).
.I mtls
takes the identity of the DTLS handshake and needs
.BR coap.dtls.enabled :
the client certificate's subject DN (RFC 4514; an ACL entry may name its
fingerprint
.I mtls:<SHA-256 hex>
instead) or
.IR psk:<PSK identity> .
.TP
.B bearer_token
Shared token accepted when
.B mode
is
.IR bearer .
.TP
.B bearer_subject
Subject that single token authenticates as.
.TP
.B jwt
Sub-map for
.BR jwt :
.B public_key
(PEM file, PKCS#1 or SubjectPublicKeyInfo, RS256),
.BR issuer ,
.BR audience ,
.B required_claim
.RI ( claim=value ;
a space-separated claim such as
.I scope
matches when it contains the value).
.I exp
and
.I nbf
are enforced with 60 s leeway. The subject is the
.I sub
claim. Without
.B public_key
the daemon does not start (exit 1).
.SS acl
Daemon-side access control per CoAP resource path. The subject is the one
.B auth.mode
yields:
.I anonymous
for
.IR none ,
the token's subject for
.IR bearer " and " jwt ,
the DTLS identity for
.IR mtls .
.TP
.B default_deny
Boolean.
.I true
denies a resource no rule names, also without any rule;
.I false
opens the unnamed rest. Not set: a resource no rule names is denied once a
rule exists or an auth mode other than
.I none
is set; with neither, every resource is open.
.TP
.B rules
List of subject-keyed rules. Each entry carries
.B subject
plus the resource-path lists
.B allow_post
(write) and
.B allow_observe
(read).
.SS metrics
.TP
.B enabled
Boolean. Turns on the admin endpoint serving
.IR /metrics ", " /catalog " and " /healthz .
.TP
.B listen
Admin listen address. Default
.IR "127.0.0.1:9093"
when
.B enabled
is true; each bridge daemon has its own port, so several run on one
host without a collision.
The key is
.BR listen ,
not
.IR address .
.SS topics (list)
.TP
.B dds_name
DDS topic name.
.TP
.B dds_type
Fully-qualified IDL type.
.TP
.B coap_uri_path
CoAP resource path. Defaults to a slug of
.BR dds_name .
.TP
.B direction
.IR in " | " out " | " bidir .
.I in
carries CoAP POST/PUT requests into DDS (the daemon creates a DataWriter),
.I out
carries DDS samples to CoAP clients through GET and Observe (a DataReader),
.I bidir
both. Default
.IR bidir .
.TP
.B qos
DDS QoS sub-map with
.BR reliability ", " durability " and "
.B history
carrying
.BR depth .
.SH EXAMPLES
See
.IR /usr/share/zerodds/configs/coap-bridged.yaml.example .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zerodds-coap-bridged (1).
